{title: If Jesus said it, I believe it}
{x_theme: faith-trust, grace-mercy}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/If Jesus said it, I believe it.docx}

{comment: Chorus}
If Jesus said it I believe it, His Word cannot lie.
If it’s written in the Bible, I’ll believe it till I die.
Though the mountains be removed and cast into the sea.
God’s Word lives’ forever, throughout eternity.

{comment: Verse 1}
A blind man cried, I cannot see.
Thou son of David, have mercy on me.
Then Jesus spoke, so soft and low.
Your eyes of faith has made you whole.

{comment: Verse 2}
Remember a man, who was in his grave.
And Jesus came by, this message he gave.
Lazarus, come forth, that’s what he said.
When they removed the stone, he rose from the grave.

{comment: Verse 3}
In my Fathers house there’s plenty of room.
And Jesus said I’m coming soon.
To catch away my waiting bride.
And take her home over on the other side.
